  // Flaming baseball (Alex's ask): a strikeout's pitch and a home run's
  // flight ball each swap in one of these two real-vector "on fire"
  // baseballs (flaming_baseball1.svg / flaming_baseball3.svg) instead of
  // the plain one every other ball uses - see pitchBallHtml/ballFlightHtml.
  // Same embed-verbatim-with-a-normalizing-transform pattern as the bat/
  // shoe icons above: each source file's own ball-only circle (its cls-2
  // navy ring path, measured directly - the surrounding flame/trail art
  // extends unevenly past it in every direction, so the ring's own bbox is
  // the only reliable "where's the ball" anchor) gives FLAME{1,3}_CX/CY/R0;
  // translate(-CX,-CY) centers that ring at this file's usual origin-
  // centered icon convention, scale(r/R0) brings it to whatever radius the
